Makes a rule that releases a commit early free the path along with the
want, as before "Keep a released commit's path until its own report":
WantList::take removes the want and records nothing, so the engine may
start a new commit of the path while the released one is still in flight,
and the released commit's report can then settle the new one (DESIGN.md
§7.5). The simulator's check for commits in flight fails the run.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_commit_released_at_a_marked_path_bars_a_second_one
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_commit_a_rule_released_keeps_its_path_until_its_own_report

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/want.rs b/crates/engine/src/want.rs
--- a/crates/engine/src/want.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/want.rs
